  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sri. Sahil S/O Shafi Abdulrehman ... vs The State Of Karnataka on 16 July, 2024 -1- Nc: 2024:Khc-D:99 Wp No. 103753 In The High Court Of Karnataka, Dharwad Bench Dated This The 16Th Day Of July, 2024 Before The Hon'Ble Mr Justice Sachin Shankar Magadum Writ Petition No. 103753 Of 2024 (Gm-Res) Between: Sri. Sahil S/O. Shafi Abdulrehman Bangali, Age: 29 Years, Occ: Business, (Managing Partner By Woop Natural), R/O. # A7 Madhura Estate, Near Madhura Apartment, Hubballi, Keshwapur, Hubballi-23. ...P (By Sri. B.D. Narasagond, Advocate) And: 1. The State Of Karnataka, Rep. By Its Secretary, Department Of Home Vidhana Soudha, Bangalore-01. 2. Commissioner Of Police, Hubballi-Dharwad, District: Dharwad-25. 3. The Police Sub Inspector, Vidyanagar Police Station, Digitally signed by Ashpak Hubballi-30, Dist: Dharwad. Kashimsa Ashpak Kashimsa Malagaladinni Location: HIGH COURT OF MALAGALADINNI KARNATAKA ...RES DHARWAD BENCH Date: 2024.07.26 15:43:17 +0530 (BY SRI. V.S. KALASURMATH, HCGP) Sri. Sahil S/O Shafi Abdulrehman ... vs The State Of Karnataka on 16 July, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/162299928/ 1 THIS WRIT PETITION IS FILED UNDER ARTICLES 226 OF THE CONSTITUTION OF INDIA PRAYING TO ISSUE A WRIT NATURE OF MANDAMUS OR ANY OTHERS APPROPRIATE WRIT, ORDER OR DIRECTIONS DECLARING THAT THE RESPONDENTS H NO AUTHORITY TO RESTRICT THE BUSINESS HOURS OF THE PETITIONER VIZ STYLE \"WOOP NATURAL\" ICE CREAM, JUICE FOODS ITEMS, AT SHOP NO.UG-9 MARVEL SIGNET, SHIRUR P MAIN ROAD, VIDYA NAGAR HUBBALLI-21, TILL 10 PM ONLY INTEREST OF JUSTICE AND EQUITY; ISSUE A WRIT OR ANY APPROPRIATE ORDER OR DIRECTIONS RESTRAININ RESPONDENTS FROM INTERFERING WITH DAY TODAY BUSINESS THE PETITIONER VIZ \"STYLE \"WOOP NATURAL' ICE CREAM, -2- NC: 2024:KHC-D:9934 WP No. 103753 of 2024 AND FOODS ITEMS, AT SHOP NO.UG-9 MARVEL SIGNET, SHIRUR PARK MAIN ROAD VIDYA NAGAR HUBBALI-21,\" ONLY IN THE INTEREST OF JUSTICE AND EQUITY AND ETC. THIS PETITION, COMING ON FOR PRELIMINARY HEARING, THIS DAY, THE COURT MADE THE FOLLOWING: ORDER 1.",
    "facts": "The petitioner is orally permitted to carry out amendment of the cause title. The petitioner has obtained a licencee from Food Safety and Standards Authority of India.",
    "arguments": "The petitioner has knocked the doors of this Court as the respondents are insisting the petitioner not to conduct his business beyond 10.00 p.m. The petitioner being a citizen having secured licence from the competent authority is entitled to carry out his business as enshrined under Article 19(g) of the Constitution of India."
  },
