        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "4. The right to conduct business is a fundamental right guaranteed under Article 19(1)(g) of the Constitution of India, which states that all citizens shall have the right to NC: 2024:KHC-D:9934 practice any profession, or to carry on any o"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "570a5ea9061748a5a4cdc2cc58f9a4ef_15",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "This right, however, is subject to reasonable restrictions that the state may impose in the interest of the general public."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "d0677f987bdd40ea8961dbc32ee45dc4_16",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "5. In the present case, the petitioner has been conducting a legitimate business with all necessary licenses from the competent authorities."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7d84766f14f44609a543b28db25239ec_17",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The Constitution ensures that a citizen cannot be arbitrarily deprived of their right to carry on a business, provided it is lawful and does not Sri."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a6c1439eedea4c1ca0ba8b6237de7c1e_18",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Sahil S/O Shafi Abdulrehman ... vs The State Of Karnataka on 16 July, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/162299928/\n2 contravene public order, morality, or health."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "ffbc41203e1b45a6bd1ee0dcd541c5da_19",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "6. The Court recognizes that while public safety is paramount, it cannot be used as a pretext to impose arbitrary restrictions on a business, especially when there are no statutory provisions supporting such restrictions."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "dd3b6c0d76da4dea9a05a46222a84228_20",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The state's responsibility to maintain law and order must be balanced against the individual's right to pursue a livelihood."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f2ae5d2d6eb84405a2ba675cfd627442_21",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "7. Thus, any restriction imposed must be reasonable, justified, and within the framework of the law."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "3e808b2977194e9d9060f601b472263a_22",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nIn this case, the respondents' insistence on early closure of the business lacks legal backing and does not constitute a reasonable restriction as envisaged under the Constitution."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "98fc31a9ce0842948ce9f371f802fe28_23",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "This Court deems it fit to protect petitioner's right to NC: 2024:KHC-D:9934 operate his business beyond the imposed hours, reaffirming the protection of fundamental rights against arbitrary administrative actions."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "3114a41da62b4f54a0bf2e04d7dafa83_24",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "8. The learned HCGP, on query as to whether there are any restrictions in carrying the business more particularly regarding time stipulation, he would fairly submit that the law does not prohibit a businessman to carry his business beyond 1"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "732321c2b7ea4635b6b47f7680ad8bc9_25",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
